This collection (INTRFC5.ZIP) contains incomplete code to decode and display
the interface section of compiled Turbo Pascal 5.0 units.  The enclosed .DOC
file describes a previous version which worked on TP 4.0 .TPU files; it seems
to apply to this one reasonably well, though the code is different.  I'm
releasing the collection to the public domain.

Note that the .TPU file format is different in every version of Turbo Pascal
released so far.  This program works (sort of) on 5.0 files only; it crashes
miserably on 4.0 or 5.5 files.

I said "sort of" above, because this program really is incomplete.  It still
has a lot of junk in it - it dumps the header, which is mostly meaningless,
for instance - and I think it fails on some .TPU files, but don't know which
ones or why.  It's being released by request from Charles Falconer - blame him
if you waste a lot of time on it.  I can't support it, since I don't use TP5.0
any more, but will attempt to answer questions.  Send them to me at

